SQL Expressions — Notes
An expression is any combination of columns, values, and operators that SQL evaluates to a single value. Expressions can appear in SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, HAVING, etc.

We use these two tables in all examples:

movies (id, title, director, year, length_minutes) boxoffice (movie_id, rating, domestic_sales, international_sales)

